CM_ BO_ 263 "Motor_04 — Engine ECU broadcast at ~50 Hz. CONFIRMED on 5G1 920 740B: bytes 3-4 LE drive cluster RPM tachometer (formula raw * 3 RPM/tick).";
CM_ BO_ 168 "Motor_12 — Engine torque + actual RPM. MQB CRC + counter required.";
CM_ BO_ 958 "Motor_14 — Engine status: gear position, engine_running flag, brake pedal, kickdown. MQB CRC + counter (constants 0xC0 from openpilot).";
CM_ BO_ 1600 "Motor_07 — Engine temps (intake, oil, COOLANT). byte 0 has QBit validity flags.";
CM_ BO_ 1607 "Motor_09 — CONFIRMED ON 5G1 920 740B AND validated against real vehicle CAN log (Alltrack 2017, May 2026). byte 0 = coolant value with linear mapping 0x80=50C → 0xED=130C (formula: temp_C = byte * 0.7339 - 43.94). Bytes 1-3 = magic 'FD FF 7F' confirmed identical on real vehicle. Bytes 4-6 = 00. byte 7 cycles between 0x13/0x18/0xC1/0x12 on real ECU (likely a counter or rolling sequence — but cluster accepts static 0xC1 too). Real ECU broadcasts at only ~2 Hz, so spoofing at 20+ Hz dominates the bus arbitration easily. Engine warmup logged: 0x86(54C) → 0xB3(87C) over 106 sec, perfectly linear with our formula. No CRC, no counter on byte 0/1.";
CM_ BO_ 1601 "Motor_Code_01 — Engine ECU heartbeat. CONFIRMED required as engine context for coolant override on 5G1 920 740B. MQB CRC with all-0x47 constants.";
CM_ BO_ 960 "Klemmen_Status_01 — CONFIRMED wakes the cluster on 5G1 920 740B (with hardware Kl.15 power on pin 16). 4 bytes. byte 2 bit 1 = ZAS_Kl_15 (ignition on). MQB CRC with all-0xC3 constants.";
CM_ BO_ 779 "Kombi_01 — sent BY THE CLUSTER per openpilot (NOT gateway). Reports current state of warning lamps, digital speed, displayed analog speed. Sending this TO the cluster has NO EFFECT — the cluster owns the message and uses its own internal state. To turn on a warning lamp, send the SOURCE message (e.g. ESP_21 with ABS error bit, Airbag_01 with crash flag, etc.).";
CM_ BO_ 1719 "Kombi_02 — Gateway → Cluster. Carries odometer (byte 0-3), fuel level liters (byte 5 low 7 bits, bit 7 = valid flag), outside temp (byte 7 with formula 0.5*x-50).";
CM_ BO_ 916 "WBA_03 — CONFIRMED on 5G1 920 740B: byte 1 high nibble drives MFA gear indicator. Values: 0x10=P, 0x20=R, 0x30=N, 0x40=D, 0x50=S, 0x60=Manual. byte 3 = M-gear digit (must be 0 for P/R/N/D otherwise cluster shows 'P4' etc.). MQB CRC.";
CM_ BO_ 1520 "Dimmung_01 — Gateway → Cluster. byte 1 = backlight target % (0-100). byte 2 = actual %. byte 1 bit 7 = night design.";
CM_ BO_ 1471 "MFSW (MultiFunction Steering Wheel) — 4 bytes. byte 0 = button code, byte 2 = sub-direction, byte 3 = 0x40 const. Per r00li: UP=06,_,01,40 / DOWN=06,_,0F,40 / LEFT=03,_,01,40 / RIGHT=02,_,01,40 / OK=07,_,01,40 / View=23,_,01,40. byte 1 = 0. NO CRC. Cluster ignores MFSW unless LH_EPS_01 (0x32A) heartbeat is also being broadcast (steering wheel 'alive' context).";
CM_ BO_ 64 "Airbag_01 — DELIBERATELY NOT TRANSMITTED by mk7-cluster-bench-controller (FORBIDDEN_IDS hard-block). Listed here for reference / passive reception only. Never spoof airbag system messages.";
